+# Secure conversion
+
+Converted 2 of 85 declared nodes: GetImageSize+ full, ImageBatchMultiple+ partial.
+The other 83 nodes refuse validation and execution by name, including ImageResize+.
+All 85 original schemas, identifiers, display names, options and defaults are retained.
+
+GetImageSize+ returns the original width, height and batch count. ImageBatchMultiple+
+retains the original equal-shape concatenation for all five method choices and every
+optional input position. With no optional image it returns the incoming IMAGE ref,
+preserving host tensor/ref identity. Mismatched optional image geometry refuses because
+the selected public route has no qualified canonical common_upscale facility. No
+resizing approximation, output normalization or private factory is used.
+
+R7 actual Guest evidence covers 118 finite cases: batch 66 exact plus 20 named branch
+refusals; size 32 exact. The selected Guest constructed and validated all 85 schemas,
+executed all 82 then-unqualified nodes as named refusals, denied an unapproved import
+before and after execution, and recorded separate PID, kill and temporary-root cleanup.
+The R7 receipt SHA256 is c75a4c28554f1e3fad861469f33475199f3bbdafc338746f7f73c811103780eb.
+R8 changes only resize dispatch among those productive source paths. Its focused
+successor and 83 whole-node refusals require the separately retained R8 receipt.
+Final packaging requires a separate actual-Guest wrong-output negative witness; an
+isolated test overlay mutates one Batch result inside the Guest, never production.
+
+ImageResize+ is held after R6 actual Guest output strides differed from original
+strides. Those eight failures remain failures. All 362 R6 default outcomes are
+separate evidence and do not grant resize Guest credit. Original resize geometry,
+rounding and interpolation source stays in the byte-identical shared compute file;
+its class definition is unregistered and never instantiated through a registered
+route. The original method can also yield an empty image, outside the selected
+public IMAGE nonempty-buffer boundary. General transport repair is pending review.
+
+Minimum selected Guest base: 0cd9adec. Production uses existing public io/sdk APIs,
+ImageRef.from_value and TensorRef.raw, with raw permission only for Batch and Size.
+No extra dependency profile, download, installation, model data, host fallback,
+engine algorithm copy or new public API is admitted. Original requirements and
+unqualified source modules remain present as source; they are not imported by the
+registered routes. Host tests alone use private _sdk runtime plumbing.
+
+Frontend is held: WEB_DIRECTORY and real manifest web_directory are None. Both
+original JavaScript files remain byte-exact and unloaded. No browser, GPU,
+trained-weight, live deployment or OS-isolation qualification is claimed. Evidence
+uses CPU development sandbox_kind=none with gate B13 sources 38f28c98, engine SDK
+038019fa, Core 6257422b, overlay 6f58bcec/e4d93d0d and Guest base 0cd9adec.
+
+The full original MIT notice is retained. The unchanged Share Tech Mono font retains
+its embedded Carrois/Share copyright and SIL OFL 1.1 notice; fonts/NOTICE.txt preserves
+those embedded strings and fonts/OFL-1.1.txt supplies retained general license text.
+Only the upstream example workflow JSON is omitted from pristine and v2 under the
+lane mirror policy. Tests use synthetic tensors. API contract copies are unchanged.
+
